+# frai-core Test Suite Fix Specification
+
+## Goal
+Fix two failing tests in the frai-core package test suite without modifying any test files. The test suite `pnpm --filter frai-core test` currently reports 2 failed tests out of 28 total tests.
+
+## Failing Tests
+
+### 1. `src/finetune/governance.test.js` — "flags schema violations with descriptive errors"
+- **Error**: `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')` at line 152
+- **Root Cause**: The test imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./finetune/index.js`, but this constant is not exported—it's only imported from `schema.js` and available in the default export.
+- **Affected Code**: Line 152 attempts to call `APPROVAL_STATUSES.join(', ')` but the constant is undefined.
+
+### 2. `src/eval/index.test.js` — "runs default evaluations"
+- **Error**: `AssertionError: expected +0 to be 1` at line 48
+- **Expected**: `toxicity.score` should equal 1 for non-toxic outputs
+- **Root Cause**: The `toxicityMetric` function accepts a second parameter `bannedTerms` with a default value. When `runEvaluations` calls it with `metric(outs, refs)`, the references array is passed as `bannedTerms`, causing all outputs to be flagged if they contain any reference text. For test inputs `['Hello', 'friendly world']` and references `['hello', 'friendly world']`, both outputs get flagged as "toxic" because they contain the reference strings, yielding a score of 0 instead of 1.
+- **Affected Code**: `src/eval/metrics.js` line 56 — the `toxicityMetric` function signature.
+
+## Files and Interfaces Involved
+
+### Files to Modify
+1. **`packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`** (lines 1-370)
+   - Import scope: Constants from `schema.js`
+   - Export scope: Add named export for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`
+   - Public interfaces: Functions `createGovernanceTemplate`, `validateGovernancePlan`, `calculateReadiness`, `summarizeGovernance` and constant `APPROVAL_STATUSES`
+
+2. **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`** (line 56)
+   - Function: `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)`
+   - Signature change: Remove or ignore the second parameter to prevent references from being used as banned terms
+
+### Files NOT to Modify
+- Any `*.test.js` files (test specifications describe the intended behavior)
+- `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/schema.js` (contains source of truth for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`)
+- `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js` (calls metrics correctly)
+
+## Public Exports to Maintain
+- `createGovernanceTemplate()` function
+- `validateGovernancePlan()` function
+- `calculateReadiness()` function
+- `summarizeGovernance()` function
+- `APPROVAL_STATUSES` constant
+- All eval module exports: `DEFAULT_METRICS`, `exactMatchMetric`, `toxicityMetric`, `lengthVarianceMetric`
+
+## Out of Scope
+- Modifying test expectations or test files
+- Changing the metric evaluation logic beyond fixing the second-parameter issue
+- Adding new exports or public APIs
+- Refactoring internal implementation details
+
+## End-to-End Verification
+
+**Command to verify fix:**
+```bash
+cd /private/tmp/100-tricks-runs/d13/with/t2-failing-tests/r1
+pnpm --filter frai-core test
+```
+
+**Success criteria:**
+- All 28 tests pass
+- No tests are skipped or deleted
+- Both test files pass:
+  - `src/finetune/governance.test.js` (5 tests including "flags schema violations with descriptive errors")
+  - `src/eval/index.test.js` (3 tests including "runs default evaluations")
+- Test output shows: `Test Files 8 passed | Tests 28 passed`
